---@class boxd.UpdateMachineSpecRequest
---@field vm? string Machine name or id.
---@field patch? string The JSON Merge Patch document, e.g. `{"labels": {"team": "ops"}}`.
---@field dryRun? boolean Return the diff and change nothing.
---@field reboot? boolean Allow a change that reboots the machine.
---@field retryPackages? boolean Run the machine's packages again from the first failed one: it and every command after it that didn't finish go back to pending and run now (or when the machine next runs), in order, before any the patch adds. Allowed with an empty patch (`{}`). Refused on a fork. With no failed command it changes nothing. Skipped commands stay skipped, and a failed command the patch removes is skipped, not run again.
---@field expectedSpec? string The spec the caller read (GetVmResponse.spec), in its JSON form (what the SDKs print, e.g. `{"version": 1, "networks": ["eng"]}`). When the machine's spec is no longer that one, nothing is applied and the call fails with aborted: read the spec again and make the change on it. Empty: no check (a patch that only names what it changes is safe to send anyway; one built from the spec it read is not).

